// Outgoing emails that settled failed or rejected, as a share of every email settled.
// Backs the "the outbox is losing mail" alert: a rejected email was refused by the provider or could
// not be sent at all, and a failed one used its last attempt or was interrupted; either way the
// tenant's administrators were told in their inbox. A handful is normal; above 5% of the settled
// emails, or more than 20 in the window, is a starting point. Sandboxed mail counts as settled, not
// failed.
customMetrics
| where name == "tellma.outbox.settled"
| extend state = tostring(customDimensions["state"])
| summarize
    lost = sumif(valueSum, state in ("failed", "rejected")),
    total = sum(valueSum)
    by bin(timestamp, 15m)
| where lost > 20 or (lost > 0 and lost * 20 > total)
